# Third-party notices and attribution

This project does not vendor any third-party code. The methods below are cited
because this work builds on them, or because they are the closest public
prior art.

## Method origins

### nikon-fw-key-tool — GPL-3.0
<https://github.com/WonderLantern/nikon-fw-key-tool>

The container layout (32-byte plaintext header, 32-space label, module directory,
two-level CRC-16/CCITT), the three-table XOR keystream with its 2^24 period, and
the keyed header digest `SHA1(decrypted_body || K8)` were established by this
project. Key recovery from constant-fill padding sectors is its method.

This repository does **not** include that code, its key files, or any firmware.
Obtain it separately if you need key recovery.

### Wonder Lantern Z30 — MIT
<https://github.com/RealCaCl2/z30-firmware-extensions>

The Z30 is EXPEED 6 like the Z6. Its patch model — standalone EG module, equal
length byte edits with expected-byte verification, code appended before the
trailing CRC, CRC recomputed and self-checked, and reuse of the stock 16:9 slot
for custom aspect ratios — is the reference this toolkit follows.

No Z30 code or artifacts are included here.

### nikon-firmware-tools
<https://github.com/simeonpilgrim/nikon-firmware-tools>

Earlier community tooling for Nikon firmware containers; consulted for framing.

